  m_Name: Plaques
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Heat Exchanger Plates
  description: The Heat Exchanger Plates are positioned at the top-center-center
    of the rocket engine and are fabricated from a specialized Plaques material,
    which offers excellent thermal conductivity and resistance to corrosion. These
    large, complex-shaped plates are responsible for transferring heat energy from
    the engine's exhaust gases to the fuel, increasing the engine's overall efficiency
    and specific impulse. Interestingly, the heat exchanger plates are designed to
    operate in a high-temperature environment, where they must maintain their structural
    integrity while facilitating the heat transfer process.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
